  <section xmlns='http://docbook.org/ns/docbook' xml:id='category-LAMBDAS'>
    <title>Lambdas</title>
    <para>A lambda is an anonymous function written with a backslash:
    `\params: body`. Parameters are space-separated. A lambda bound to a name
    and applied to arguments is monomorphized at the call site for those
    argument types, so the same lambda works at any argument type.</para>

    <section xml:id='tests-LAMBDA-APPLICATION'>
      <title>Lambda Application</title>
      <para>A lambda bound to a name can be called like a function.</para>
      <informaltable frame='none'>
